a:["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"What licence covers most of the code?"}],["$","td",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0"}],", the Functional Source License, converting to Apache 2.0 two years after each version ships"]}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"What covers the rest?"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Business Source License 1.1, on two modules: metrics and persistent workers"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Does the binary enforce the split?"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No. No licence key, no check, no gate, no feature flag"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Is the free build limited in size, workers, or team?"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Does it contact Trace Machina?"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No"}]]}]]}]
b:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"two-licences-one-repository","children":"Two licences, one repository"}]
c:["$","p",null,{"children":["The repository root carries ",["$","code",null,{"children":"LICENSE"}],", the Functional Source License 1.1 with\nan Apache 2.0 future grant. Its restriction is narrower than most people\nexpect on first reading: it permits everything except a ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Competing Use"}],",\nwhich the licence defines as making the software available to others in a\ncommercial product or service that substitutes for Forge, substitutes for\nsomething Trace Machina already offers using it, or offers substantially\nsimilar functionality."]}]
d:["$","p",null,{"children":"Named as explicitly permitted, in the licence text itself: internal use and\naccess, non-commercial education, non-commercial research, and use in\nconnection with professional services you provide to someone else who is\nthemselves complying."}]
e:["$","p",null,{"children":"The practical read for most readers is that running Forge as your own\nbuild farm (for a team, for a company, in production, commercially) is\ninternal use, and internal use is permitted. Reselling a managed Forge\nservice is what the licence is written to prevent."}]
f:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-brand/40 bg-brand-soft/40 text-foreground","role":"note","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M12 16v-4M12 8h.01M12 22c5.523 0 10-4.477 10-10S17.523 2 12 2 2 6.477 2 12s4.477 10 10 10Z"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"The Apache conversion clock is per version, not a single date"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The future grant is effective \"on the second anniversary of the date we make\nthe Software available.\" That clock runs per released version, not once for\nthe project. Version 1.6.5 converts to Apache 2.0 two years after 1.6.5 was\npublished; a version released next month converts a month later. No\nfuture date exists on which the whole repository becomes Apache; there is a rolling\ntwo-year trailing edge."}]]}]]}]
10:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-business-source-licensed-modules","children":"The Business Source Licensed modules"}]
11:["$","p",null,{"children":"Five files in the tree carry a Business Source License 1.1 header instead of\nthe repository licence. They form two modules:"}]
12:["$","div",null,{"className":"relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Module"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Files"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"What it is"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Metrics"}],["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-util/src/metrics.rs"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Every OpenTelemetry instrument Forge declares: the cache counters and histograms, the execution stage and result metrics, and the attribute sets attached to them"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Persistent workers"}],["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-worker/src/persistent_worker/{mod,pool,live_worker,protocol}.rs"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Bazel's persistent-worker protocol: keeping a compiler process warm across actions instead of starting one per action"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
13:["$","p",null,{"children":"Their headers say the same thing, verbatim:"}]
14:["$","$L48",null,{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},"tabIndex":"0","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M 6,1 C 4.354992,1 3,2.354992 3,4 v 16 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 12 c 1.645008,0 3,-1.354992 3,-3 V 8 7 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 20.707031,6.2929687 l -5,-5 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 15,1 h -1 z m 0,2 h 7 v 3 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 3 v 11 c 0,0.564129 -0.435871,1 -1,1 H 6 C 5.4358712,21 5,20.564129 5,20 V 4 C 5,3.4358712 5.4358712,3 6,3 Z M 15,3.4140625 18.585937,7 H 16 C 15.435871,7 15,6.5641288 15,6 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" /></svg>","children":["$","$L49",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"// Use of this module requires an enterprise license agreement, which can be"}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"// attained by emailing contact@forge.com or signing up for Forge"}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"// Cloud at app.forge.com."}]}]]}]}]}]
15:["$","p",null,{"children":"(The header still names Forge Cloud, which is no longer offered; the\nmanaged option today is Forge Enterprise, and the email address is the\nroute to either agreement.)"}]
16:["$","p",null,{"children":["The wording matters. It is a licence obligation attached to ",["$","em",null,{"children":"use of the\nmodule"}],", which is a different question from whether you may run the binary at\nall. You may run the binary; whether you may exercise those two modules in a\nshared, production or commercial setting depends on a separate agreement."]}]
17:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"nothing-in-the-binary-enforces-any-of-this","children":"Nothing in the binary enforces any of this"}]
18:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-50/60 text-foreground dark:bg-amber-500/10","role":"alert","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400","aria-hidden":"true","children":"$0:data:0:rsc:props:children:0:props:children:2:props:children:3:props:children:0:props:children"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"No licence check exists anywhere in the codebase"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["No licence key field exists in the configuration schema. No startup\nvalidation reads one. No runtime gate wraps either module. Searching the\nwhole tree for enforcement turns up exactly five hits: the five header\ncomments listed above, and nothing else. Both modules are compiled\nunconditionally and both run by default. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"You can be out of compliance\nwithout ever seeing an error, a warning, or a log line."}]," The boundary here\nis legal, not technical, and the software will not help you find it."]}]]}]]}]
19:["$","p",null,{"children":"This is not an oversight to route around. It is the reason this page exists:\nif you rely on the binary to tell you which features you are entitled to, it\nwill tell you that you are entitled to everything."}]
1a:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h3","id":"metrics-are-always-on","children":"Metrics are always on"}]
1b:["$","p",null,{"children":["No configuration turns instrumentation off. The meter provider\nis constructed unconditionally during startup and installed globally, and the\nscheduler and store layers call into the licensed instruments on their normal\npaths: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"simple_scheduler_state_manager.rs"}]," records completed executions,\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"memory_awaited_action_db.rs"}]," records stage transitions, and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"cache_metrics_store.rs"}]," records every cache operation."]}]
1c:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"NL_OTEL_ENDPOINT"}]," is often mistaken for the switch. It is not. Setting it\nchooses a load-balanced gRPC channel for the OTLP exporters; leaving it unset\nmeans the exporter builds its own channel to the OTLP default instead. Either\nway the instruments are declared and recorded. What changes is where the\nexport attempt goes, not whether measurement happens."]}]
1d:["$","p",null,{"children":["The consequence for licensing is that \"we don't use metrics\" is not a\nconfiguration you can be in. What you can choose is whether you ",["$","em",null,{"children":"consume"}],"\nthem: whether a collector is running, whether dashboards and alerts are built\non them, whether they are part of how your team operates the cluster. That\nconsumption is what the licence is about. See\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/observability","children":"Observability"}]," for the pipeline itself, and note that\npage's own ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/observability#do-metrics-require-a-commercial-licence","children":"licence callout"}],"."]}]
1e:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h3","id":"persistent-workers-activate-from-the-action-not-from-your-config","children":"Persistent workers activate from the action, not from your config"}]
1f:["$","p",null,{"children":["No ",["$","code",null,{"children":"persistent_worker"}]," key exists anywhere in the configuration schema;\nsearching ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config"}]," for it returns nothing at all. The module is\nreached entirely from the action's own platform properties:"]}]
20:["$","div",null,{"className":"relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Property"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Values"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Effect"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"supports-workers"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"1"}]," activates; anything else, or absent, does not"]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"The only trigger. The worker checks this before every action"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"requires-worker-protocol"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"proto"}]," (default) or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"json"}]]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Wire format. Any other value (or a persistent worker that cannot be started) makes the worker log and fall back to ordinary one-shot execution of the action"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
21:["$","p",null,{"children":["Those properties come from your build tool. Bazel sets them on rules that\ndeclare worker support: Java and Scala compilation, TypeScript, and anything\nusing ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ctx.actions.run"}]," with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"execution_requirements"}]," asking for workers.\nA Bazel build that already uses persistent workers locally will exercise\nthe licensed module remotely the first time it runs an affected action, with\nno Forge-side opt-in and nothing in your configuration mentioning it."]}]
22:["$","p",null,{"children":"Because there is no config surface, the pool's behaviour is fixed at\ncompile-time defaults:"}]
23:["$","div",null,{"className":"relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Behaviour"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Value"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Tunable?"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Live workers per key"}],["$","td",null,{"children":["4 (matching Bazel's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_max_instances"}]," default)"]}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Idle shutdown"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"5 minutes without a request"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Requests before recycling a worker"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"200"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
24:["$","p",null,{"children":["Two actions share a worker process when their ",["$","em",null,{"children":"worker key"}]," matches: same\nresolved executable, same startup-flag prefix (the arguments before the first\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"@response-file"}],"), and same wire format. The full picture, including what\nisolation you give up, is on\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/persistent-workers","children":"Persistent workers"}],"."]}]
25:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-the-open-source-build-does-not-limit","children":"What the open-source build does not limit"}]
26:["$","p",null,{"children":"Nothing in the code artificially constrains scale. Specifically, there is no\ncap on cache size, stored object count, action throughput, connected worker\ncount, or number of people using the cluster; no trial period, expiry date, or\ntime-limited mode; and no registration, activation, or account required to\nstart the binary."}]
27:["$","p",null,{"children":["Nor does the binary report anything home. The only outbound HTTP clients in\nthe tree belong to storage backends you configure yourself (the S3-compatible,\nGCS and Azure object stores), and the only other egress is to the other\nbackends you configure (Redis, MongoDB, ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," stores), gRPC to the peers in\nyour own cluster, and the OTLP exporters. Those exporters send to whatever endpoint you point\nthem at, which is your collector; if you point them somewhere else, that is\nyour configuration doing it, not a default."]}]
28:["$","p",null,{"children":["The limits you will actually hit are the operational ones (file descriptors,\ndisk, memory, scheduler backpressure), and those are documented in\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/troubleshooting#limits-that-block-instead-of-erroring","children":"Troubleshooting"}],"\nand ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/runbooks","children":"Runbooks"}],"."]}]
29:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-cloud-and-enterprise-add","children":"What Enterprise adds"}]
2a:["$","p",null,{"children":"The honest answer, from inside this repository, is that the paid tier is not\na different codebase, so this documentation cannot enumerate its feature list\nby reading the source. What can be said accurately:"}]
2b:["$","p",null,{"children":"It carries the licence for the two Business Source modules in shared,\nproduction and commercial settings, which for most teams running metrics-driven\noperations is the substantive difference, since as shown above there is no way\nto run without touching that module."}]
2c:["$","p",null,{"children":["It removes the operational work. The whole of the\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate","children":"Operate"}]," section (the deployment shape, the metrics\npipeline, the eviction sizing, the incident runbooks) describes work that a\nmanaged tier does instead of you. That is the trade\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/getting-started/shared-cache","children":"Shared cache"}]," frames as an operational-cost\nquestion (control-plane compute, CAS storage, worker compute, and the engineer\nhours to run it) rather than a licence question."]}]
2d:["$","p",null,{"children":["For what Enterprise includes, its pricing, and what support attaches to it, the\nsources of truth are ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"https://forge.com/pricing","children":"forge.com/pricing"}],"\nand the ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"https://forge.com/license","children":"licence page"}],". Meaningful contributors\nto the project may be eligible for waivers on the Business Source modules;\nask the maintainers before relying on one."]}]
